  "id": "magnitude-production",
  "term": "magnitude production",
  "definition": "Magnitude production is a direct time-judgment task in which a person is given a duration value, such as a number of seconds, and tries to produce an interval of that length. In psychophysical research, it is paired with magnitude estimation to study how perceived duration relates to actual clock time.",
